  {
    "index": 3,
    "hash": "CbBDMcGeDuehZ17erYrZRVihzaI=",
    "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:19:09.271Z",
    "action": {
      "type": "SET_CONTENT",
      "input": {
        "content": "The reactor's own open-issue list records this as gap 4a. `KyselySyncDeadLetterStorage` implements `remove(id)` and `removeByRemote()`, but **`ISyncManager` has no methods for dead-letter management**, so nothing above the storage layer can retry or resolve one.\n\nThe consequence for an operator: a document that dead-letters is quarantined until someone reaches past the sync manager into storage. There is no supported \"retry this dead letter\" call, no way to drain a remote's dead letters as a batch through the public interface, and therefore no UI that can offer it without depending on storage internals.\n\nThis pairs badly with the one failure mode that is guaranteed *not* to converge on its own \u2014 two reactors writing conflicting auth-scope operations, where the replica whose stream ran ahead dead-letters the arrival and holds a different policy until an application reconciles it. The reconciliation the design assumes has no interface to perform it through.\n\n## Provenance\n- `packages/reactor/sync-gaps.md` \u2014 4. Dead Letter Handling \u203a 4a\n\n_Extracted from the Powerhouse repository at **v6.2.2-dev.74**._",
        "updatedAt": "2026-09-03T07:19:09.271Z"
      },
      "timestampUtcMs": "2026-09-03T07:19:09.271Z"
    }
  },
